# Restored 2026-08-24: the Phase-0 harness setup OVERWROTE the skill's original
# .gitignore with three lines (printf > instead of merge), dropping the state/,
# evals/_out/ and .pytest_cache/ protections. Rebuilt from the documented keep-list
# the receiving toolkit repo preserved, plus this project's one new rule.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
evals/_out/
state/
.regression/

# NOTE: reference/geocode_cache.json is NOT ignored, though it once was. enrich.py sets
# SEED_DIR = <skill>/reference and MERGES all three reference/*.json caches into every
# run as read-only seeds (work-dir copies win), so ignoring one of them contradicted the
# code and the keep-list below. Runs write to the WORK dir - main() repoints CACHE_DIR -
# so these files do not grow per run; they are seeded deliberately, via seed_geocode.py.
# keep (committed), i.e. the whole shipped skill:
#   SKILL.md, KNOWN-DEFECTS.md, NOTICE, .gitignore
#   helpers/           the pipeline + the build-time dataset tools
#   reference/*.md     the contracts SKILL.md links
#   reference/*.json   the read-only seed caches enrich.py merges (geocode, poi_osm) plus
#                      regions_cache.json, which is the documented EXAMPLE of the
#                      region-research cache shape, not run data
#   prompts/*.md       the canonical dispatch-prompt templates
#   templates/         canonical.schema.json + record_schema.json
#   evals/             the whole suite (run_all.py is the bar for a skill edit)
#   assets/            the frozen template + VERSION + the i18n packs + the *.json /
#                      *.json.gz datasets and ledgers + placeholder.uri +
#                      reference_screenshots/ (a documented placeholder for the
#                      G-visual baselines, see reference/visual-qa.md)
#   vendor/            the native PyMuPDF wheel the Cowork sandbox lacks (~24 MB, and
#                      deliberately NOT in the integrity manifest - a truncated wheel
#                      must degrade to fitz_shim, never hard-fail a run)
# assets/integrity.json is the authoritative list of build-critical tracked files
# (helpers/, prompts/, templates/, assets/) - do not let this comment drift from it.
